{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition","id":908932,"title":"A Little help for Vampire vs Werewolf battle on Second edition.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-06T23:45:47-07:00","id":908932,"title":"A Little help for Vampire vs Werewolf battle on Second edition.","content":"The title can be a little misleading. We are running a Requiem second edition LARP. a coming battle with a pack of Pure has come up. I have bought the Second ed Book but its physically impossible to skim through it in time,.So i come to you fine ladies and gents of the Internet for help!<br /> <br /> What i need<br /> Char sheets for <br /> 1 scout subtype. <br /> 1 warrior <br /> 1/elder /spirit magic one. <br /> <br /> I need full builds not suggestions and if possible a little explanation how to utilise the powers of the different forms.<br /> <br /> The vampire team is full of mental/social disciplines. so a little explanation on the how the clash of wills mechanic apply in both Dominate / Majesty Disciplines and what can pierce through Obfuscate will be most helpful<br /> <br /> I know its a lot but any help will do wonders and thank you all in advance !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T00:03:50-07:00","id":908945,"title":"","content":"Rough experience level? Starter characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T00:10:08-07:00","id":908949,"title":"","content":"10 to 20 experiences. the biggest level of discipline is three biggest Blood potency is 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T00:15:13-07:00","id":908952,"title":"","content":"Okay, I for staters how much 2e knowledge do you have? Have you checked out some of the NPCs in the 2e book (in the back sections)? <br /> <br /> Also, if you are looking for a physical confrontation be wary. Werewolves got a <b>huge</b> boost from 1e, Gauru form in particular is a terror, even a group of physically inclined Vampires would struggle against a newly changed Werewolf in war form. So if you were picturing a down and dirty fight to the death sort of battle, you might want to reconsider.<br /> <br /> As for Clash of Wills, that's a Storyteller call, but an easy one to make. If two magical powers conflict, such as a Gift that detects enemies and Obfuscate, that's a Clash of Wills. If two characters attempt to dominate the same subject and give them conflicting commands, that's a Clash of Wills. For the most part these situations are pretty obvious when they arise, and the handing is very straight forward. If magic conflicts with magic, Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T00:55:00-07:00","id":908967,"title":"","content":"We are well versed in the ways of the rules of the Second Edition we even have adapted them to the Larp Format.<br /> <br /> We want to add werewolves in our Chronicle so we want to be as precise as possible.<br /> <br /> How what are the differences between the Pure and the Forsaken battle wise? 1 Pure is enough for a &quot;put fear in their minds &quot; encounter? What avenues we could we take in the battle resolution?<br /> <br /> A WW masquerading as a casualty to surprise them?<br /> <br /> A ww as a rampant monster for a pure physical battle?<br /> <br /> if they don't have silver weapons they are boned but are mental disciplines easy to stop them . Is there another modifier except the resolve +Primal Urge roll to resist being affected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T01:53:23-07:00","id":908985,"title":"","content":"I don't know that mental effects bother them in gauru as they are focused on murder. If one death rates and kills the whole pack goes into death rage. Each turn in war form they heal all bashing and lethal damage, and their bite now does lethal damage to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:06:39-07:00","id":909354,"title":"","content":"It'd be helpful to know context.<br /> <br /> Urban vs Rural makes a big difference as does the general climate between the Pure and Forsaken in the area, not even to mention what types of threats are the normal for the Pure to take on. Are these nomadic bikers? A inbred backwoods Klan banjo-pluckers? Are they the wolves of Wallstreet, so to speak?<br /> <br /> The most important thing to know about Pure is they run in much larger packs than Forsaken, 15-20 Uratha deep. all connected via a Totem which is way more powerful than Forsaken would even dare deal with. The Totem, would be a lethal threat all by itself, and you should start there, Rank 3-4 Spirit, if you have the Chronicles of Darkness book. Because the Spirit is more powerful it demand greater devotion and sacrifice, and could be said to be the boss of the relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-07-2016, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:42:09-07:00","id":909380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=908967#post908967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are well versed in the ways of the rules of the Second Edition we even have adapted them to the Larp Format.<br /> <br /> We want to add werewolves in our Chronicle so we want to be as precise as possible.<br /> <br /> How what are the differences between the Pure and the Forsaken battle wise? 1 Pure is enough for a &amp;quot;put fear in their minds &amp;quot; encounter? What avenues we could we take in the battle resolution?<br /> <br /> A WW masquerading as a casualty to surprise them?<br /> <br /> A ww as a rampant monster for a pure physical battle?<br /> <br /> if they don't have silver weapons they are boned but are mental disciplines easy to stop them . Is there another modifier except the resolve +Primal Urge roll to resist being affected?</div> </div> </div> </div>In killing form werewolves recieve bonuses to resisting psychic effects. There's also a gift that increases psychic defense. In the book it's called Fearless Hunter.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, technically. It causes class of wills agaisnt all psychic effects including obscufate 1s occlusion. And if the caster passes, any other members of the pack subject to the same effect autopasses. Also in clash of wills... technically it gets an additional bonus to the clash, meaning that the Vampire will be at a disasvantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as close combat, werewolves are pretty hard to kill due to their regeneration being kind of ridiculous. You can't just have your troupe attacking a different member each. If you want to win, you need to take advantage of focus firing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh and in combat forms they apply full defense versus firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:00:16-07:00","id":909552,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I just wrote this up real quick. You said 10-20 so I just went with 15. As has been said, attempts to deter or alter a werewolf's behaviour during Kuruth suffer twice their Primal Urge as a penalty. This is in addition to their normal resistance roll. Garou in general is difficult to deal with. Enemies lose their skill bonus to defense and the Werewolf regenerates all damage per turn (as well as +5 health and +3 stealth, and +2 weapon modifier and initiating grapples after dealing damage). I avoided a bunch of spirit stuff because Vampires just don't really have any ways to handle that. Like, any at all. So your group probably isn't prepared for it. I mostly just went with renown because powers are fun, but might have over did it. I also didn't bother finishing the totem because I got lazy and it ideally shouldn't actually show up except perhaps when using Totemic Empowerment.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I went with a more Urban scout/infiltrator type than the traditional sneaky wolf. The idea is that the scout can use his gifts to change his gender, his face/body or even appear as a vampire. He can unlock any doors and appear as anyone, essentially. He can absorb information directly from any store of knowledge, from a library to a computer, can learn the names and social merits of anyone he comes across. So he is the infiltrator and information gatherer. He is also difficult to pin down, due to Hit and Run, Exit Strategy and his Warding gifts.<br /> <br /> The Warrior is pretty straightforward. He fights and kills. He's pretty strong so it's unwise to take him on directly. In Garou form he's likely unkillable by any of the group, so indirect tactics and baits are better options. He can increase his strength and damage, reduce damage, and double his speed to chase down anything he comes across. He can tear through most structures with his claws. In Death Rage he is The Juggernaut.<br /> <br /> The Elder can use Reflected Facets to double up on Berserker's Might if necessary, can improve the entire pack's initiative to the highest roller's, can predict in vague terms impending doom, as well as various other insight gifts to plan or outmaneuver enemies. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If he succeeds at resisting any Mental Disciplines, the entire pack also succeeds at it.He is also always aware of his packmate's general location and emotional state, and can speak to them telepathically. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They are really dangerous to fight as a group, partially because of him. He's also no slouch at fighting, especially in Garou form.<br /> <br /> The trick is to separate them somehow. If they lose any one member, they become woefully unprepared for an assault of some kind. Using human allies, the police or other political or social influence is likely to be pretty effective as well. Dominating a member on his own might also work. They don't really have a lot of defenses for obfuscate either. I may have made them too effective, I don't know.<br /> <br /> If you're rushed for time, I'd focus on understanding Death Rage, the 5 forms and their uses, and the gifts and rites the antagonists use. Again, I avoided spirit magic largely because it's just hard to deal with.</span></span><br /> <br /> Also, make sure to look at the Ivory Claw <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Sacred Hunt</a> because it's relevant and probably useful for tracking down vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ivory Claw Scout </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cFace Stealer\u201d</span></span></b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Talents: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Information gathering, Urban Infiltration, Disruption, Trapping, Escape</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Personality</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Overconfident, Preening, Fond of a challenge</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Challenger, </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bone: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hedonist</span></span><br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attributes</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Resolve 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence 1, Manipulation 3, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Academics 2, Investigation 2, Politics 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Larceny 2, Stealth 3, Weaponry 3 (Knives)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Empathy 1, Persuasion 2, Socialize 2 (Etiquette), Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2 (Disguise)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Renown</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cunning (2), Honor (2), Purity (1), Wisdom (1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pusher<br /> Indomitable<br /> Direction Sense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fading</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resources (2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Light Weapons (2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Totem (3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Language: First Tongue</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gifts</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Death </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Cunning):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cold Embrace</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Knowledge </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Honor, Wisdom):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Know Thy Prey, Sift the Sands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evasion </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Purity, Wisdom): Hit &amp; Run, Exit Strategy</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warding </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Cunning, Honor):</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maze Ward, All Doors Unlocked</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Change</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (Cunning, Honor): Skin Thief, Luna\u2019s Embrace</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rites</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sacred Hunt</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">15 xp: 9 on Renown, 3 on Death Gift, 2 on Sift the Sands, 1 on Wolf Gift</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free: 2 Totem, 1 Politics, 1 Persuasion, Language: First Tongue, Indomitable, Direction Sense</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Predator King Warrior \u201cHungers for Battle\u201d</span></span></b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Talents: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fighting, Killing, Tracking, Intimidation</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Personality:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Relentless, Short Temper, Single Minded, Loyal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blood:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Destroyer, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bone</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Confidant<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Urge</b> 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attributes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence 1, Wits 2, Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crafts 2, Investigation 2, Occult 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 3 (Foot Chase), Brawl 4 (Bite, Grappling), Stealth 2, Survival 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animal Ken 2, Intimidation 4, Streetwise 1 </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Renown</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Glory (3), Purity (2), Wisdom (1)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demolisher (3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fleet of Foot (3)<br /> Indomitable<br /> Direction Sense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dedicated Locus (1)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Totem (3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Language: First Tongue</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">+ Primal Urge (-5)</span></span><b