nt-family:Arial\">Alpha. </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bone: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Guru<br /> <b>Primal Urge</b>: 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attributes</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strength 3, Dexterity 1, Stamina 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Presence 3, Manipulation 3, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Skills</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Academics 2, Crafts 1, Medicine 1, Occult 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 2, Brawl 3 (Garou)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Empathy 3 (Detecting Lies), Expression 3 (Howling), Intimidation 1, Persuasion 3, Subterfuge 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Renown</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cunning 2, Glory 3, Honor 1, Wisdom 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">War Cry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Residential Area (2)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Indomitable<br /> Direction Sense</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dedicated Locus (1)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Totem (3)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Language: First Tongue<br /> <br /> + Primal Urge (-5)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gifts</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inspiration (Honor, Glory): Pack Triumphs Together, Fearless Predator</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rage (Cunning, Glory): Incite Fury, Berserker\u2019s Might</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Insight (Cunning, Honor, Glory, Wisdom): Prey on Weakness, Echo Dream, Read the World\u2019s Loom, One Step Ahead</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pack (Cunning, Wisdom): Reflected Facets, Pack Awareness</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rites:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Totemic Empowerment, Chain Rage</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">16 xp: 15 on Renown, 1 on Wolf Gift</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free: 2 Totem, 1 Expression, 1 Subterfuge, Language: First Tongue, Indomitable, Direction Sense<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Totem: Rex Urbana<br /> Rank 2<br /> Boon: Indomitable, Direction Sense<br /> Aspiration: Learn and use every back alley of the territory<br /> Ban: Territory can never be left unattended<br /> Influences:<br /> Numina: Stalwart, Regeneration, Awe, Blast</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:18:39-07:00","id":909562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=909380#post909380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In killing form werewolves recieve bonuses to resisting psychic effects.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, not quite. That's Death Rage that they get the bonus. Regular Garou recieves no such bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also a gift that increases psychic defense. In the book it's called Fearless Hunter.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, technically. It causes class of wills agaisnt all psychic effects including obscufate 1s occlusion. </div> </div> </div> Actually, if you want to be technical, it doesn't do that - you'd need an ST to make that call. It merely gives a bonus to resistance rolls. Nothing says a Clash of Wills. Personally, I'd say this Facet no more allows a Clash of Wills than the Indomitable merit would.<br /> <br /> &quot;Technical&quot; implies a strict reading of the rules with exact wording. Unless there are writers that can confirm this, I don't think its something we can consider RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:04:14-07:00","id":909603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=909562#post909562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, not quite. That's Death Rage that they get the bonus. Regular Garou recieves no such bonus.<br /> <br /> Actually, if you want to be technical, it doesn't do that - you'd need an ST to make that call. It merely gives a bonus to resistance rolls. Nothing says a Clash of Wills. Personally, I'd say this Facet no more allows a Clash of Wills than the Indomitable merit would.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Technical&amp;quot; implies a strict reading of the rules with exact wording. Unless there are writers that can confirm this, I don't think its something we can consider RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah you do need to make the call for it, it however is implicit. Still you can make arguments for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:32:48-07:00","id":909625,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't think it's implicit at all. It would make sense to call for it, but Clash of Wills isn't part of the mechanic of the Facet, and it doesn't<i> prevent </i>anything, only gives bonuses to resist. Specifically it gives a bonus to dice rolls against powers, so if there is no dice roll to contest it could be argued that it does nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:07:41-07:00","id":909657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=909603#post909603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah you do need to make the call for it, it however is implicit. Still you can make arguments for them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not implicit, though, in either case. I personally don't see it implied anywhere, and, given that we have vampire PCs and werewolf NPCs, its better to err on the side of PCs.<br /> <br /> Like Amravanti, I can see where people would make that call. I can also see where people say the opposite. Unless a writer says that was their intent, I'm going to have to go with what makes the better story for the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-07-2016, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T03:44:38-07:00","id":909959,"title":"","content":"Fire Touched pack- Scout is an ex-military specialist clever and good sense but in the heat she's still a soldier who is very good at what she does, a real danger to Vampire Havens and her gifts not only allow her to track seamlessly but detect other kinds of Supernaturals making her a huge danger who can also take care of herself physically. The Warrior is a bit too full of herself always trying to assert her dominance and authority to the pack due to a hard life on the streets. She's a terror who focuses on all out attack, but that can leave her open especially since she's always going out alone. But the Spirit Elder is the hardest, safe in the Hisil or back home she can coordinate her pack with her pack gifts or bring mortal agents to the equation due to her long standing relationship with organized crime. She can use her gifts from afar often using the scout as her eyes and ears. If that isn't bad enough she's made friends with several fire spirits. One gift could make an entire block into an inferno. These three could be a hard team to deal with for any group.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Scout:</b></u></span><br /> Blood: Soldier (She gains 1 willpower when ignoring own safety for a leaders orders, gains all when she goes into death rage or partakes in a hunt to fulfill an Alpha's orders against her own good sense) <br /> Bone: Guru (Gains 1 Willpower when someone succeeds by following her advice, she regains all Willpower when her practical advice leads her pack to an alternate solution to the hunt.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attributes:</b></u><br /> Intelligence 2 Wits 3 Resolve 3<br /> Strength 2 Dexterity 3 Stamina 2<br /> Presence 1 Manipulation 2 Composure 3<br /> <br /> <u><b>Skills:</b></u><br /> Occult 2, Investigation 3<br /> Larceny 4 (Security systems), Brawl 2, Athletics 2, Stealth 3, Firearms 2<br /> Persuasion 2 (pack), Empathy 2, Subterfuge 4 (Detecting Lies)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits:</b></u><br /> Fleet of Foot 1<br /> Contacts (Ex-Military) <br /> Sleight of Hand <br /> Totem 2<br /> Language: Spirit Tongue <br /> Fading <br /> Tactical Shifting 3<br /> <br /> <u><b>Renown:</b></u><br /> Wisdom 2 Cunning 2 Purity 1<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Urge 1</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>Gifts:</b></u><br /> Insight (Cunning)(Purity)<br /> Inspiration (Wisdom)<br /> Hunting (Wisdom) (cunning)<br /> Change: (Wisdom)<br /> <br /> <b>10 exp:</b> 6 exp on renown; 4 on Larceny <br /> Free: 1 Occult, 1 Subterfuge, Totem 2, Spirit Tongue 1<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Warrior</span></b></u><br /> Blood:Alpha (She gains 1 Willpower when she puts order over free thinking logic, and gains all when she uses the force of her bestial nature to keep others in line)<br /> Bone:Lone Wolf (She gains 1 willpower when she acts independantly of the pack to solve a pack problem, and gains all willpower when her pack is on the hunt and she subverts their plans and solves the problem alone)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attributes:</b></u><br /> Intelligence 2 Wits 2 Resolve 2<br /> Strength 4 Dexterity 2 Stamina 4<br /> Presence 2 Manipulation 3 Composure 2<br /> <br /> <u><b>Skills:</b></u><br /> Crafts 2(Jury-Rigging), Medicine 1, Occult 2<br /> Athletics 3, Brawl 4, Stealth 2, Survival 2 (Urban)<br /> Subterfuge 3(Prey), Intimidation 2, Streetwise 3 <br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits:</b></u><br /> Status 2 (A Local Gang)<br /> Increase primal Urge (+5)<br /> Language: First Tongue<br /> Relentless Assault 4<br /> Totem 2<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Urge 2</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>Renown:</b></u><br /> Wisdom 1 Glory 2 Cunning 1 Honor 1 <br /> <br /> <u><b>Gifts:</b></u><br /> Inspiration (Glory)<br /> Rage (Glory) (Cunning) (Honor)<br /> Hunting (glory) <br /> Insight (Wisdom)<br /> <br /> <b>15 exp:</b> 6 exp on renown; 4 Strength; 4 Stamina, 1 to increase Relentless Assault to 4<br /> Free: First tongue, 2 Totem, 1 Occult and Subterfuge<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spirit Elder</span></b></u><br /> Blood:Fox (She gains 1 willpower when she drops everything and flees the scene; All willpower when she falls into Karuth to escape a violent situation)<br /> Bone:Community Organizer ( She gains 1 Willpower if she convinces a group to focus on internal problems rather than external ones; all willpower when she convinces her pack to eschew the hunt)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Attributes:</b></u><br /> Intelligence 3 Wits 2 Resolve 2<br /> Strength 2 Dexterity 2 Stamina 2<br /> Presence 3 Manipulation 3 Composure 2<br /> <br /> <u><b>Skills:</b></u><br /> Investigation 2, Occult 3, Politics 4 (Organized Crime), Academics 3(Research)<br /> Survival 2(Hisil), Brawl 4, Stealth 1<br /> Socialize 3, Empathy 1, Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> <u><b>Merits:</b></u><br /> Language: First Tongue<br /> Totem 2<br /> Allies 3 (Organized Crime)<br /> Safe Place 2<br /> Dedicated Locus 2<br /> Resources 3<br /> Allies 1 (fire Spirits)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Renown:</b></u><br /> Wisdom 3 Cunning 1 Purity 2 Honor 1 Glory 1<br /> <br /> <b>Primal Urge 2</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>Gifts:</b></u><br /> Elements: (Glory) (Purity)<br /> Insight: (Honor)<br /> Knowledge (Honor) (Wisdom) (Purity)<br /> Pack (Cunning) (Wisdom)<br /> Hunt (Purity)<br /> <br /> <b>20 Exp</b>: 15 on Renown; 5 on Primal Urge<br /> Free: 2 Totem, First tongue, 1 Subterfuge and Occult<br /> <br /> I didn't include Totem or Rites as they are more fun if personalized to chronicle but assume one of them has Sacred hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:01:08-07:00","id":923598,"title":"","content":"Just give your vampires guns with silver bullets. That should level the playing field rather quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T05:25:26-07:00","id":929669,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for your answers. <br /> <br /> After some initial skirmises, the player got the message and lets just say that the price for Silver in Athens has risen up to about as much as gold.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Moreover, they special ability of entering the Shadow Realm has he following abilities. You can either get in wherever you want but you can get out in a place of power. or they can enter in a place of power and exit whenever they want.<br /> <br /> Correct? <br /> <br /> Also, i am interested in ideas about how 2 packs of Pure would do a crusade to rid a big city of vampires. Gifts? Shamanistic Rites&gt;? <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your answers its quite helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:24:23-07:00","id":929682,"title":"","content":"Fire-Touched would spontaneously combust havens from the safety of the shadow realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:32:29-07:00","id":929685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=929669#post929669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot for your answers. <br /> <br /> After some initial skirmises, the player got the message and lets just say that the price for Silver in Athens has risen up to about <br /> <br /> Also, i am interested in ideas about how 2 packs of Pure would do a crusade to rid a big city of vampires. Gifts? Shamanistic Rites&gt;? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would recommend downloading the adventure under a blood red Moon. That illustrates what a full on lupine assault on a vampire city would look like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:38:22-07:00","id":929690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=929685#post929685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would recommend downloading the adventure under a blood red Moon. That illustrates what a full on lupine assault on a vampire city would look like</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a SAS? Link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T07:01:24-07:00","id":929697,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3433/Under-a-Blood-Red-Moon?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Looks like an Old World of Darkness adventure.</a><br /> <br /> I imagine Predator Kings would have a fun time of it, ripping apart ghoul families and wrecking so-called 'hunting grounds' of vampires. They probably don't like them much to begin with, since they hate people who dishonor the hunt.<br /> <br /> Ivory Claws would probably have the most vampire-like battle, with them using their influence among politicians and the rich to stymie the vampires. They would probably have the advantage of being able to act during the day and being some of those politicians and rich themselves. Their sacred hunt benefit would be spectacular for spotting out ghouls and other vampires, 'The Ivory Claws Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to sense the familial or community relationships anyone he encounters has with his prey. The direct blood relations of the prey have difficulty protecting the prey from the Uratha. Any attempts to block or hinder the werewolf, or to refuse to provide information, suffer a penalty equal to the Uratha\u2019s Primal Urge.'<br /> <br /> Fire-Touched would probably have it the easiest, though. It will be interesting to see if they still hold their hatred against liars, which might add to the fervor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:44:34-07:00","id":930056,"title":"","content":"Yes, under a blood red moon is an old world of darkness adventure on drivethrurpg.com. I would recommend spending a few extra bucks to get Chicago chronicles 2 which has that and Chicago by night 2 which is a great template for a vampire city.<br /> <br /> Who says that interactions between werewolves and vampires need to ever get violent. The vampires might only need to make simple eye contact to dominate a pack into submission","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T17:49:55-07:00","id":930058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=930056#post930056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says that interactions between werewolves and vampires need to ever get violent. The vampires might only need to make simple eye contact to dominate a pack into submission</div> </div> </div> </div>Because trying something like that is going to lead to violence. You might as well say that they wouldn't fight because the werewolves would just kill them while they slept so there'd be no vampires to fight with.<br /> <br /> They work much better as peers. They are the two closest of all the splats, in terms of famous folklore and being predators and having to hide their identity from hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T18:26:08-07:00","id":930076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/908932-a-little-help-for-vampire-vs-werewolf-battle-on-second-edition?p=930056#post930056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says that interactions between werewolves and vampires need to ever get violent. The vampires might only need to make simple eye contact to dominate a pack into submission</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion of a vampire holding eye contact with multiple Uratha at once is hilariously incongruent with biology. Nevermind willingly falling to Kuruth, good luck dominating them then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}